  "id": "COMPOUND:14699 - PROTEIN:6305",
  "verbalization": "Megestrol is implicated in the relationship with Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are ultimately directed toward this subunit. The evidence suggests that megestrol acts as a target for DNA polymerase eta, which in turn is targeted by (2S,3S)-3,3',4',5,7-Pentahydroxy Flavanonol and (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-[[(2R,3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-4-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-6-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenoxy)oxane-3,4,5-triol. These compounds are all known to interact with the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, indicating a potential pathway where megestrol indirectly influences this enzyme through its interaction with DNA polymerase eta. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same subunit suggests a broader role for DNA polymerase eta in the regulation of Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, possibly through a mechanism involving enzymatic activity or structural modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex interplay between DNA polymerase eta and the vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, emphasizing the importance of these interactions in cellular processes.",
